{"id":"acclaimedgames-rs9","title":"Optimize metadata refresh performance","description":"Improve the performance of the weekly metadata refresh process. Current full refresh takes 62-72 minutes for ~1000 games.\n\n## Current Bottlenecks\n1. **Wikipedia processing is SEQUENTIAL** - processes 1 game at a time (~38 min)\n2. **HLTB default concurrency too low** - defaults to 1 in fetch_hltb_data.py (5 in refresh_all_metadata)\n3. **Commands run sequentially** - IGDB → Wikipedia → HLTB → ProtonDB\n\n## Dependencies Between Steps\n- HLTB depends on Wikipedia: HLTB uses Wikidata HLTB IDs from WikipediaGameData (populated by Wikipedia step)\n- ProtonDB is independent (uses Steam App ID, not Wikipedia data)\n\n## Proposed Optimizations\n1. Add asyncio concurrency to Wikipedia fetching (like HLTB/ProtonDB already have)\n2. Increase HLTB default concurrency from 1 to 5 in the command itself\n3. Run ProtonDB in parallel with HLTB (ProtonDB is independent)\n4. Consider bumping ProtonDB concurrency from 5 to 10\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Full refresh completes in under 45 minutes (vs current 62-72 min)\n- No increase in API rate limit errors\n- All tests pass","status":"closed","priority":2,"issue_type":"epic","created_at":"2026-01-04T17:29:27.368455-05:00","created_by":"rchibana","updated_at":"2026-01-04T17:52:08.036652-05:00","closed_at":"2026-01-04T17:52:08.036655-05:00"}
